// EXPECT: E0223 — `<<` on an `enum_flags` (ADR-0043 §3)
// A flags enum accepts `& | ^ ~` and not the shifts: `Perm.READ << 1` would produce `WRITE`
// by an accident of the numbering, which is the same objection ADR-0041 §6 used to refuse
// ordering. The note says so rather than claiming bitwise operators need an integer, which
// would be misleading for a type that accepts the other four.
Perm :: enum_flags {
    READ;
    WRITE;
}

main :: () {
    p := Perm.READ << 1;
}
